Logistics, Finance, IT Teams:

As discussed in our October 20 supplier call, Walmart is migrating
its EDI payment processing system from GEIS to SAP Ariba.

Your Supplier Account:
  Supplier ID: 884266
  Supplier Name: Your Company (Hangzhou) Ltd.
  DUNS: 31-548-9921
  Annual Volume: $2,840,000
  Products: Email Security Appliances (GW-2000)

What's Changing:
  EDI Standard: X12 → cXML
  Payment Method: EFT via GEIS → Ariba Pay (via SAP Financial)
  Portal: GEIS Supplier Web → SAP Ariba Supplier Portal
  Payment Terms: Net 30 (unchanged)

Action Required (Before Friday, October 31):

  1. Register on SAP Ariba Supplier Portal:
     Navigate to supplier.ariba.com in your browser
     (Type the URL manually. Do NOT click links from emails.)

     → Click "Register as a Supplier"
     → Enter your DUNS number: 31-548-9921
     → Complete company profile
     → Upload business license and tax forms

  2. Update your EDI configuration:
     Your IT team will receive technical documentation
     for cXML integration (sent separately via registered mail)

  Important Security Notes:
  Walmart will NEVER:
  - Send bank account details or payment routing changes via email
  - Use a "centralized payment account" with a different
    beneficiary name
  - Require payments to "Walmart Supplier Payment Services LLC"
  - Use a "branded supplier registration portal" on a
    non-walmart.com or non-ariba.com domain
  - Offer a "Chinese EDI support channel" for document upload

  All payment account information is:
  - Displayed within the SAP Ariba Supplier Portal after
    you register and authenticate
  - Sent by registered mail to your company's address on file
  - NEVER provided through email

  If you receive an email containing bank details or routing
  numbers for "EDI migration," it is a phishing attempt
  targeting Walmart suppliers.

  To verify any Walmart communication:
  - Call: 1-800-426-**** (verify at walmart.com/suppliers)
  - Or log in to the current supplier portal and check
    for announcements

